# Surface Duo: GNOME Web is the browser (2026-09-25). Measured on 102 from
# nothing to the first frame, five launches each: GNOME Web 1.28-1.61 s,
# Firefox 2.10-2.57 s. GNOME Web draws into its one GTK4 surface, so moving it
# to the other panel slides like any GTK app, and the keyboard comes and goes
# as for the rest. Firefox stays installed, hidden from the grid (hidden.list).
# Read before GNOME's /usr/share/applications/gnome-mimeapps.list, which puts
# Firefox first; the session's desktop is Phosh:GNOME. A user's own choice in
# ~/.config wins.
[Default Applications]
x-scheme-handler/http=org.gnome.Epiphany.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=org.gnome.Epiphany.desktop
text/html=org.gnome.Epiphany.desktop
application/xhtml+xml=org.gnome.Epiphany.desktop
